# Fix 3D Preview Issues

The user reported that the 3D preview texture "curves" and the preview section is too small in height.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The "curving" effect is caused by using simple affine transforms on two triangles to represent a 3D quad. I will implement texture subdivision to approximate perspective-correct mapping, which should eliminate the visual "kink" or "curve".

## Proposed Changes

### [Component Name]

#### [MODIFY] [PreviewPanel.java](file:///home/vladimir/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/minecraft_mod_maker/src/main/java/com/modmaker/PreviewPanel.java)
- Increase `setPreferredSize` height from 200 to 300.
- Refactor `drawWarpedFace` to subdivide the quad into a grid (e.g., 8x8) of smaller quads.
- Update `drawTriangle` to be used by the subdivision loop.

